<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Ruiz de Azagra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1186</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Ruiz de Azagra was a Navarrese noble who obtained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albarracin">Albarracín</a> around 1170 from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mardanish">Ibn Mardanish</a>, the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> he had served. He resettled the town with Christians and held it as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-mother-of-jesus">Virgin Mary</a> rather than of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> or Aragon, founding the semi-independent Lordship of Albarracín and its bishopric.</p></div>
